  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Le Migon is a beach restaurant set in a former fishermen's cabin, at the very end of Pampelonne beach, below the Camarat lighthouse. The establishment's website describes a rustic hut with a terrace facing the sea. The cuisine is Provençal and Italian: grilled fish, seafood platter, bouillabaisse, linguine with clams, beef tataki, and a snack corner (panini, sandwiches, hamburger) for picnics on the sand.</p>

      <h2>Dog, terrace and practical information</h2>
      <p>The Ramatuelle tourist office listing (offer updated on 15/05/2026) classes the restaurant among the establishments that accept animals. The restaurant has 160 seats including 130 on the terrace: with a dog, the terrace facing the sea is the natural place; in winter, the dining room has a fireplace. Booking is stated as compulsory on the tourist listing. The website also offers a welcome from 8am for breakfasts and brunches, takeaway dishes and a boat shuttle from the anchorage.</p>
      <p>À la carte, the tourist office announces €20 to €50 and a dish of the day at €30 (period from 5 April 2026 to 3 January 2027). Payment is by bank card, American Express or cash. Parking is signposted on site and nearby.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: out of season, the terrace and the fireplace allow a quiet lunch facing the sea, without the summer crowds.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is at the southern end of Pampelonne, on the Camarat lighthouse side. The neighbouring beach is a Ramatuelle beach: the rule for dogs depends on the season and the municipal order, to be checked before going down onto the sand.</p>
    </div>

